# Live test on the accepted handoff15 build (#104), 2026-11-04
# via SSH, /sys/class/graphics/fb0/blank

=== T0 (before) ===
blank=0 uptime=280 fwloads=5 recover=4
irq: 3745 -> 3805 in 5 s   (~12 IRQ/s, healthy)

=== T1: echo 4 > fb0/blank  (panel off) ===
blank=1 fwloads=6 recover=5
[286.278] sky-fwinfo: fw_ver=0x18 ~=0xE7 raw=18e710240438099c
[286.282] sky-state: raw=a00101000000 (ret=0, poll 0)
[286.940] Firmware reset failed (raw=a00101000000 want 0xa1..0xaf ret=0).
[286.945] sky: IC late in reaching ReK, continuing
[286.949] Touch IC fw loaded ok
[286.956] sky-report[0]: 777777777777 state=a00101000000 irq_line=0
irq: 3816 -> 3816 in 5 s   (0 IRQ/s: IC never reached NORMAL_RUN)

=== T2: echo 0 > fb0/blank  (panel back on) ===
blank=0 fwloads=6 recover=5
[305.167] sky-panel: vendor-long-write init; PPS sent, err=0     <- panel re-prepared
[305.169] sky-panel: dcs read id=3 [c0 11 00] pwr=1 [9c]
irq: 3816 -> 3816 in 6 s   (still 0 IRQ/s)

# Diagnosis: the recovery that ran while the panel was off "succeeded" per
# FWINFO and set DOWNLOAD_COMPLETE although the IC never left INIT (state 0xA0).
# On the next panel prepare internal_pm_resume() then saw
# SUSPEND clear + DOWNLOAD_COMPLETE set and did nothing, and the health poll
# only reacted to 0xFD/0xFE/0xFF, so a stuck-in-INIT IC was never noticed.
# Touch stayed dead until reboot.
